            <div xml:id="d541">

                <pb facs="0562" n="550" xml:id="pg550"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.311F1 Advisory Committee/1062a:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-03T22:00:00-05:00">December 3,
                            1941—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5624. Your 5767, November 29. It is understood that Salter has telegraphed London
                    concerning our proposal referred to in paragraph 6 (prices) of Department’s 5346
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">5446</hi>], November 26 and has asked for
                    instructions. If you have not already done so, please advise the appropriate
                    British authorities that you are expecting instructions in this connection and
                    suggest that their reply to Salter be delayed until you have had an opportunity
                    to discuss the matter with them. In the meantime, a reply concerning the
                    questions raised in your 5767 will be sent as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
